  "recommended_action": "Stay at rung 3 and run rung 2 alongside it. (1) Control room and operator: consider the RF jammer D-JAM now. T-1 has PID and PVID, a live control link, and is closing on Z-HQ (814 m, about 75 s). A warning alone, with the pilot unknown, is unlikely to work in time (ROE-1.5). It needs operator plus control-room approval (ROE-4.1). Before use: confirm with the tower that no crewed aircraft is within 3 km of the target (ROE-5.2). No notice reports one, but the data does not show aircraft positions. Plan for loss of link: the drone may hover, land, return, or continue on its own toward Z-HQ (ROE-5.3). Pair jamming with a security search for the pilot. (2) Rung 2 now: warn. Notify base security and the control room (pilot unknown, ROE-6.5). Watch the drone's return path. If the pilot is found on base, send security (ROE-6.1). If off base on U.S. land, call Harborview Police (ROE-6.2, N-17). If on the water, call the Coast Guard (ROE-6.3, N-18). (3) Keep S-GIM on T-1 to hold PVID. If T-1 is about to reach Z-HQ or acts hostile, the threat becomes CRITICAL and the control room re-plans (ROE-3.1). The interceptor is the next option only if the jammer fails or is blocked."
}

